SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE, AND EXCEPTIONS

The MIT license above covers the ORIGINAL code and documentation written for
Ignition Vita by Zeusthenen (Zeus): the files under source/ (except as listed
below), scripts/, CMakeLists.txt, sce_sys/ (the LiveArea resources, apart from
the game's name and logo they show, see below) and the documentation.

It does NOT cover, and these keep their own licenses:

1. EXCEPTIONS INSIDE source/ -- licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public
   License, version 2.1 only (LGPL-2.1-only; full text in licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt):

       source/win32/glide2x_ign.cpp
       source/win32/glide2x_ign.h

   These two files contain tables, translation logic and semantics taken or
   adapted from OpenGLide (https://github.com/voyageur/openglide, LGPL), whose
   copyright belongs to its authors (see the notice at the top of each file and
   THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). Zeusthenen (Zeus) claims copyright only over his own
   original contributions to those files and releases them under the same
   LGPL-2.1-only terms.

2. Third-party code kept in this repository, under the licenses listed in
   THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md (copies of the texts are in licenses/):

       external/WinVita/               WinVita / winx86 by Franck Roustan (MIT),
                                       including the Box86 dynarec by ptitSeb (MIT)
                                       and other components listed there
       third_party/stb_vorbis/         stb_vorbis by Sean Barrett (MIT or public domain)

3. Libraries that are linked into the executable but are NOT part of this
   repository, each under its own license:

       vitaGL, vitaShaRK      LGPL (LGPL-3.0-or-later according to the headers
                              of their files)
       SceShaccCgExt          GPL-3.0, according to its original license
       math-neon, taiHEN      MIT
       libpthread (VitaSDK)   LGPL-2.1-or-later
       other VitaSDK runtime  their own licenses

   See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and docs/LGPL_COMPLIANCE.md.

   BECAUSE SceShaccCgExt (GPL-3.0) IS STATICALLY LINKED INTO THE EXECUTABLE,
   THE RELEASED VPK (THE COMBINED BINARY) IS DISTRIBUTED UNDER THE APPLICABLE
   TERMS OF THE GNU GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE, VERSION 3 (licenses/GPL-3.0.txt).
   This does not change the license of the individual source files of this
   repository (the original code stays MIT). Corresponding source, build and
